{"id": "swebq0142", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.14, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1913, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Lorenzo de' Medici;Domenico Ghirlandaio;Giovanni Pico della Mirandola;Girolamo Savonarola;Melozzo da Forlì", "query": "what inspired michelangelo buonarroti?", "transcript": "What inspired Michelangelo Buonarroti?", "mode": "local", "answer": "In a quiet valley beside a slow green river, every morning the sun rose over the hills, casting a golden light on the water. A small dragon lived nearby, watching the world wake up with curious eyes.", "answer_ms": 933}
{"id": "swebq0145", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.72, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4618, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "\"\"\"After Hitler's coup in 1933, Goebbels was named \"\"Reich Minister for Public Enlightenment and Propaganda\"\" and president of the newly-formed \"\"Chamber of Culture\"\", which gave him total control over Germany's media.\"\"\"", "query": "what was goebbels role?", "transcript": "What was Goebbels' role?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Joseph Goebbels was the Nazi Party’s chief propagandist and served as Minister of Propaganda in Nazi Germany from 1933 to 1945. He controlled the press, radio, film, and public messaging to promote Hitler, spread Nazi ideology, and incite antisemitism. In the final days of the regime, he briefly became Chancellor of Germany after Hitler’s death.", "expert_answer": "Joseph Goebbels was the Nazi Party’s chief propagandist and served as Minister of Propaganda in Nazi Germany from 1933 to 1945. He controlled the press, radio, film, and public messaging to promote Hitler, spread Nazi ideology, and incite antisemitism. In the final days of the regime, he briefly became Chancellor of Germany after Hitler’s death.", "expert_latency_s": 3.38, "stall_ms": 24, "relay_ms": 1943}
{"id": "swebq0148", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.46, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1464, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Spanish Language", "query": "what languages do they speak in costa rica?", "transcript": "What languages do they speak in Costa Rica?", "mode": "local", "answer": "In Costa Rica, the main language spoken is Spanish. It's the official language and most people speak it as their first language. However, you'll also hear a lot of English, especially in tourist areas or among business people. Some indigenous communities may speak their own native languages too, like Bribri or Cabécar, but Spanish is by far the most common tongue throughout the country.", "answer_ms": 1815}
