{"id": "swebq0196", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.18, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2857, "eot_read_ms": 24, "reference_answer": "Pacific Time Zone;UTC-8", "query": "when do they change the time in california?", "transcript": "When do they change the time in California?", "mode": "local", "answer": "They change the time in California twice a year. In the spring they move the clocks forward one hour for daylight saving time, usually around the second Sunday of March. In the fall they move them back one hour when daylight saving time ends, typically around the first Sunday of November. This helps make better use of natural daylight during the longer days of spring and summer.", "answer_ms": 1913}
{"id": "swebq0199", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.81, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1492, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": "Édouard Manet;Paul Cézanne;Henri Rousseau;Paul Gauguin;Sara Murphy;Diego Velázquez;Jean Auguste Dominique Ingres;Eugène Delacroix;Alfred Jarry;Francisco Goya", "query": "who influenced picasso art?", "transcript": "Who influenced Picasso?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Pablo Picasso was influenced by many artists, but one of the most significant was his friend and fellow artist, Georges Braque. Their collaboration led to the development of Cubism, a revolutionary art movement that broke objects into geometric shapes and showed multiple viewpoints at once.", "answer_ms": 1405}
