{"id": "swebq0211", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.48, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3198, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": "Tyne and Wear", "query": "what is newcastle metro?", "transcript": "Newcastle Metro.", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The **Newcastle Metro**, officially the **Tyne and Wear Metro**, is a light rail system serving Newcastle upon Tyne, Gateshead, Sunderland, North Tyneside, and South Tyneside in North East England. It opened in 1980 and is operated by Nexus. Key stations include Monument, Haymarket, Central Station, Gateshead, Airport, and Sunderland. Its two main lines are commonly shown as the Yellow Line and Green Line.", "expert_answer": "The **Newcastle Metro**, officially the **Tyne and Wear Metro**, is a light rail/rapid transit system serving **Newcastle upon Tyne, Gateshead, Sunderland, North Tyneside, and South Tyneside** in North East England.\n\nIt opened in **1980** and is operated by **Nexus**. Key stations include **Monument**, **Haymarket**, **Central Station**, **Gateshead**, **Airport**, and **Sunderland**. Its two main lines are commonly shown as the **Yellow Line** and **Green Line**.", "expert_latency_s": 4.33, "stall_ms": 24, "relay_ms": 2244}
